From 8ddc5548d568b75e57b2724aa54eda99f48f5a3f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Axis Dev <axis-dev@example.com>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 11:11:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] feat: redesign Axis landing page layout
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Restructures /axis into a proper product-tour layout, keeping the
site's existing light theme and tokens throughout:

- Hero: centered single-column headline/copy (no illustration),
  CTAs, and a small trust line
- Screenshot showcase: floating dashboard + activity panel directly
  below the hero
- Modules: three full alternating text/screenshot rows (Invoicing,
  Ledger, Inventory), each with a scroll-triggered reveal
  (RevealOnScroll, sliding in from the text side), plus a closing
  3-card row for HR/Team Access/Multi-org. Screenshot blocks are
  clearly TODO-commented placeholders ready to swap for real product
  screenshots.
- Connected-workflow band: simplified to a clean 4-card grid,
  removing a screenshot that duplicated the new Ledger row
- Pricing: three-tier card preview matching the finalized plan
  entitlements, linking to /axis/pricing
- FAQ: converted from static cards to a real accordion using the
  existing Radix-based ui/accordion component
- Removed a trust bar that listed Trevix Media, Next Level Store,
  Excom, and Etihad as Axis customers — these are Regent's internal
  dogfooding businesses, not paying Axis clients, and presenting
  them as customer social proof was inaccurate. Axis currently has
  no external customers, so no trust/logo section is shown.
